```text
PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Public Services Committee was held on Tuesday, May 21, 2024, in Committee
Room 104 and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 pm. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Scott Roybal, Chairman. Pete Layboum. Dr. Rinne. and Tom
Segrave (via Zoom).
AGENDA ITEMS
13.
ORDINANCE —3 READING
— Amending Sections 1.4.3 Defined Tents and 5.8.8
Accessory Buildings of the Unified Development Code, clarifying Detached Buildings.
Dr. Rinne joined the meeting at 12:03 p.m. during discussion of item #13.
Dr. Rinne moved to approve on 3 and final reading, seconded by Mr. Laybourn. Dr. Rinne moved
to amend section 5.8.8(j) to remove all references to “5 foot” and replace with “3 foot”, seconded
by Mr. Laybourn. Motion to amend carried by unanimous voice vote. Main motion, as amended
carried by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report. Chairman Roybal
and committee members Laybourn and Segrave commented on the item. Public comments were
made by Brandon Swain and Michael White.
14.
ORDINANCE _3rd READING
— Amending Ordinance No. 4519 amending the Official
Zoning Map of the City of Cheyenne changing the zoning classification from HI Heavy
Industrial, AG Agricultural, and County A-2 to LI Light Industrial for land located west of
Burlington Trail and south of and adjacent to HR Ranch Road.
Dr. Rinne moved to approve on 3”’ and final reading, seconded by Mr. Laybourn. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Clerk’s Note: Original motion was made to approve on 2’d reading with all members voting “YES”
upon correction to “3”’ and final reading”, Mr Segrave experienced technical difficulties and an
affirmative vote was not audible.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report.
Ii
ORDINANCE _3rd READING
- Amending Subsections 6.5.4.b.3 Incentives / Bonus,
6.5.4.b.4 Creative Sign Program. and 6.5.8.j Billboards of the Unified Development Code,
to restructure sign incentives and bonuses by modifying allowances for signs near interstate
highways, allowances for shared signs, eliminating the Creative Sign Program, and
clarifying applicability of certain billboard allowances.
```

