```text
Dr. Rinne moved to approve on 3rd and final reading, seconded by Mr. Laybourn. Dr. Rinne moved
to amend to reduce the height and space allowance when in close proximity to residential
properties (which include signs within 350 linear feet of the property line of a duplex, single-
family dwelling, or townhouse located in a residential zone district, the following modifications to
requirements apply:
1) 20’ minimum clearance: 2) 40’ maximum height; 3) 100 square feet
maximum area), seconded by Mr. Layhourn. Motion to amend carried by unanimous voice vote.
Maing motion, as amended, carried by unanimous voice vote.
Seth Lloyd, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and committee members
Rinne and Segrave commented on the item.
16.
ORDINANCE —3”’ READING
— Amending Section 5.1.5 of the Unified Development
Code to allow for up to three stories for detached dwellings, semi-attached dwellings, and
attached dwellings.
Dr. Rinne moved to approve on 3”’ and final reading, seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Seth Lloyd, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and committee members
Layboum and Segrave commented on the item.
20.
ORDINANCE _20c READING
— Amending Chapter 5.78, Towing and Wrecker Recovery
Operations, of Title 5, Business Licenses and Regulations, of the Municipal Code of the
City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, modifying provisions governing towing and wrecker
recovery operation licensure and the Police Department’s towing and wrecker recovery
operation rotation list. (SPONSOR
— MR. ROYBAL)
Dr. Rinne moved to approve on 2nd reading, seconded by Mr. Laybourn. Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Lieutenant Dan Long, Police Department, provided a staff report.
Chairman Roybal and
committee member Laybourn commented on the item. Public comments were made by Laramie
County Commissioner Gunner MaIm and David Rose, Big .41’s Towing, and representative of
towing operators of Cheyenne.
24.
RESOLUTION
— Adopting the fee schedule setting the approved towing service rates for
towing charges related to calls for service by the Cheyenne Police Department made
pursuant to the tow rotation list. (SPONSOR
— MR. ROYBAL)
Dr. Rinne moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Layboum. Motion carried with Mr. Layboum and Dr.
Rinne voting “YES” and Mr. Segrave voting “NO’.
Lieutenant Dan Long, Police Department, provided
a staff report and committee members
Laybourn. Rinne, and Segrave commented on the item.
Public comments were made by Jeny
Hargraves, Wreckers Towing: and David Rose, Big Al’s Towing and President of Wyoming
Towing & Recovery Professionals.
```

### Page 3 of 3

```text
27.
RESOLUTION
— Authorizing the Mayor and the City Clerk to sign a Final Plat for
Cheyenne Business Parkway, Thirteenth Filing, City of Cheyenne, Laramie County,
Wyoming (located west of Christensen Road and south of and adjacent to Campstool
Road). (SPONSOR - MR. ROYBAL)
Dr. Rinne moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Laybourn. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White. Planning & Development Department. provided a staff report and Brad Emmons,
AVI P.C. provided additional information.
28.
RESOLUTION
— Authorizing the Mayor and the City Clerk to sign a Final Plat for
Centennial Heritage. 3” Filing, City of Cheyenne, Laramie County, Wyoming (located east
of Savannah Drive and south and north of Raleigh Drive). (SPONSOR
— MR. ROYBAL)
Dr. Rinne moved to adopt with staff conditions: I) exception to block size; and 2) subdivision
standards, seconded by Mr. Laybourn. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and Seth Lloyd,
Planning & Development Department, provided clarification regarding staff conditions. Casey
Palma, Palma Land Planning, provided additional information. Committee member Rinne
commented on the item.
29.
RESOLUTION
— Approving sanitary sewer service, by Outside User Agreement, for
Laramie County, for the property known as the Archer Complex (south of the 1-80 and
Archer Parkway Interchange). (SPONSOR
— MR. ROYBAL)
Dr. Rinne moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Laybourn. Motion carried with Mr. Laybourn and
Dr. Rinne voting “YES” and Mr. Segrave voting “NO”.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and Seth Lloyd,
Planning & Development Department provided additional information. Committee members
Layboum, Rinne, and Segrave commented on the item.
Public comments were made by Molly
Bennett, Laramie County Public Works Director; Charles Bloom. City of Cheyenne Planning &
Development Department Director: Ben Ilornok, TC Solutions; Laramie County Commissioner
Gunner Maim: and Michael White.
There being no further items for the agenda to come before the Public Services Committee, the
meeting was adjourned at 1:24 p.m.
Submitted by.
I
Jennifer McClelland
Executive Assistant to the Cheyenne City Council
```
